  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (1E,5R,10S,11S,14S)-4-ethyl-10,14-dihydroxy-5-[(1S)-1-hydroxyethyl]-11-methoxy-12-oxa-4-azatricyclo[9.2.1.02,5]tetradec-1-en-3-one, appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to the PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1. This is supported by evidence from three distinct paths, each showing the compound as a target of different molecules that in turn target CDC2L1. Path 1 links the compound to Phenylalanine-4-hydroxylase, which is a known target of Cryptophycin 23, while Path 2 and 3 show the compound as a target of EDD domain proteins, which are also targets of RA-Xii and Itaconic Anhydride, respectively. These pathways suggest that the compound may act as a modulator or inhibitor of CDC2L1 through different molecular mechanisms. The evidence is consistent across the three paths, indicating a potential role for the compound in regulating CDC2L1 activity. However, the exact mechanism by which the compound influences CDC2L1 remains unclear, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the nature of this relationship.",
